        "id": "ch5_6-1",
        "text": "Summary\nIn this chapter, we introduced different levels of testing for software applications. We also\nevaluated two test frameworks ( unittest and pytest ) that are available for Python test\nautomation. We learned how to build basic- and advanced-level test cases using these two\nframeworks. Later in the chapter, we introduced the TDD approach and its clear benefits\nfor software development. Finally, we touched base on the topic of CI, which is a key step in\ndelivering software using agile and development-operations ( devops ) models.\nThis chapter is useful for anyone who wants to start writing unit tests for their Python\napplication. The code examples provided provide a good starting point for us to write test\ncases using any test framework.\nIn the next chapter, we will explore different tricks and tips for developing applications\nin Python.",
